cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SpaxNMF, please cite the software release and the associated paper when available."
title: "SpaxNMF: Regularized Non-negative Matrix Factorization for IFU Cubes"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "de Souza"
    given-names: "Rafael S."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7207-4584"
    affiliation: "University of Hertfordshire"
identifiers:
  - type: url
    value: "https://github.com/RafaelSdeSouza/SpaxNMF"
repository-code: "https://github.com/RafaelSdeSouza/SpaxNMF"
license: "MIT"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-03-12"
abstract: >-
  SpaxNMF is an R package for IFU cube decomposition with regularized
  non-negative matrix factorization. The package provides helpers for
  reshaping cubes, reconstructing components, and preserving cube-side
  metadata through fitted outputs.
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - IFU spectroscopy
  - MaNGA
  - R
  - torch
  - non-negative matrix factorization
  - spectral decomposition
